%erg 0.1
Title: findTicketsDir refuses cross-worktree store resolution
Created: 2026-05-30
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-30T20:00Z MinhHaDuong created
2026-05-30T20:30Z claude planned: storeWorktreeConflict helper in main.go, osExecutable seam for tests, one-liner in spec + manualPreamble; erg update behavioral change noted

--- body ---
## Context

If you are in a worktree, erg should not get out of it. The current
auto-discovery candidate chain (binary-dir, tickets/ under cwd, cwd)
silently resolves to a store in the main checkout when invoked from
a linked worktree via the installed binary. The result is a ticket
written to -- or read from -- the wrong worktree with no indication
that anything is wrong.

The principle: a store resolved outside the current git worktree is
always a surprise. Surprises should be errors, not silent choices.

## Design

After auto-discovery selects a candidate store, check whether that
store is inside the same git worktree as cwd:

  - Same worktree (or git unavailable, or cwd is not in any worktree):
    proceed as today.
  - Different worktree: exit 1 with a diagnostic:

      erg: store found at /path/to/main/tickets/ (branch: main)
           but cwd is in a different worktree (branch: t0194)
           pass an explicit DIR to override

Applies to ALL commands that resolve a store (findTicketsDir and
resolveDir): list, ready, check, next-id, new, close, log, label,
unlabel, archive, rm, migrate. Explicit DIR always bypasses the check
-- the caller has declared intent.

Offline-safe: if git is unavailable the worktree boundary cannot be
determined; skip the check and proceed (same degrade pattern as banner).

## Spec change

Add one sentence to the Store auto-discovery section of spec-erg-v1.md
and update manualPreamble in main.go (which generates erg-manual.md):

  "If the resolved store is in a different git worktree than the
  working directory, erg exits with an error. Pass DIR explicitly
  to override."

## Implementation notes (from planning)

- Extract `storeWorktreeConflict(store string) error` helper in main.go.
  Calls worktreeTopFor on store and cwd; returns nil if either is empty
  or they are equal; returns formatted error otherwise.
- Add `var osExecutable = os.Executable` seam for testing the binary-dir
  candidate path without building a real binary.
- filepath.Abs the resolved candidate before passing to the check --
  findTicketsDir currently returns relative paths.
- erg update also calls findTicketsDir (update.go:130) and will now
  correctly refuse from a linked worktree. Note in PR body.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] findTicketsDir() calls worktreeTopFor on both the resolved
      store and cwd; if both are non-empty and unequal, returns an
      error with the diagnostic above
- [ ] resolveDir() propagates the check (wraps findTicketsDir)
- [ ] Explicit DIR argument bypasses the check in all commands
- [ ] No failure when git is unavailable (offline-safe)
- [ ] No failure when cwd is not inside any git worktree
- [ ] erg list, erg new, erg ready all fail with the diagnostic
      in a test where store and cwd are in different real git worktrees
- [ ] spec-erg-v1.md and manualPreamble updated with the new rule
- [ ] make check passes
